# OpenSquad UI (soft tooling)

Read [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) for full tokens. Follow this when changing frontend chrome.

## Skill combo (do not load all remote skills every time)

1. **Anthropic frontend-design** — brief before big UI changes
2. **Impeccable quieter / polish** — softer spacing, type, motion
3. **garden `linear`** — hairline panels, radius ≤16, one muted accent
4. **qiaomu** — Chinese copy / 盘古之白 only when editing zh strings
5. **Pro Max / Taste** — not for routine app chrome (landing only for Taste)

## Hard rules

- Use semantic Tailwind colors (`bg-bgLight`, `bg-panel`, `border-border`, `text-textMain`, `text-textMuted`, `primary`). No hardcoded purple/indigo brand gradients.
- Theme colors only via `themeStore` / `themeEngine` CSS vars.
- Radius: 6 / 12 / 16 max for chrome. Soft single-layer shadow; prefer hairline borders.
- Motion 150–200ms ease-out; honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Modal headers: quiet panel + border — not full-bleed primary bars.
- Nav active: soft primary tint, not loud filled blocks.
- Ban: emoji-as-icons, glow shadows, multi-accent rainbow, AI landing-page clichés in product UI.

## Soft pass checklist

Before finishing a UI change: quieter contrast, consistent 8px spacing rhythm, focus rings via `ring-primary/25`, light + dark both readable.
